For when you finish:



I had this idea based on reading the following code:


```swift
      if (statusStrength(world, actor, "stunned") > 0
        || statusStrength(world, actor, "rooted") + effectStrength(world, actor, "frost_nova") > 0) {
        world.remove(actor, MoveIntent);
        continue;
      }
```





Basically that all of these are trying to communicate effectively the same thing -- namely that the target is prevented from moving.



Therefore, what I wondering is if there isn't an internal representation of immmobilized, with potentially a little bit of source metadata.



Anyhow -- this is a future facing idea that we can think about after we closeout the three that we're working on now.&#x20;



And again -- just an idea from reading ONE piece of code -- you're free to disagree with me.



\:-)

